## QUBO → Ising Conversion (the critical piece)

The QUBO uses `x ∈ {0,1}` variables. The circuit operates on `Z ∈ {+1,−1}` spins.  
Substitution: **x_i = (1 − Z_i) / 2**

```
Linear QUBO term h·x_i:
  → Ising linear on Z_i:  −h/2       (constant +h/2 dropped)

Quadratic QUBO term J·x_i·x_j:
  → Ising linear on Z_i:  −J/4
  → Ising linear on Z_j:  −J/4
  → Ising ZZ on Z_i⊗Z_j: +J/4       (constant +J/4 dropped)
```

Gate decomposition:
- Single Z: `RZ(2·γ·h)` on qubit i
- ZZ interaction: `CX(i,j) → RZ(2·γ·J) on j → CX(i,j)`

